---

== 🚀 Overview

**Linux Zero** is a professional, modular C-based system engineered for high-performance, low-latency kernel-level security auditing and telemetry on Linux. It combines hardware-assisted tracing, performance counters, virtualization-based MSR interception, and eBPF tracepoint monitoring with an ultra-fast lock-free shared memory architecture.

---

== ✨ Key Features

* 🔬 *Hardware-Assisted Tracing (Intel PT):* Real-time execution flow tracking using Processor Trace via `perf_event_open` and mapped auxiliary buffers.
* 📊 *Performance Monitoring Counters (PMC):* Direct hardware counter collection (CPU cycles, instructions, cache misses, branch misses, and raw counters).
* ⚙️ *MSR Interception & Filtering:* Virtualization-based control using KVM (`/dev/kvm`) to filter and intercept critical Model Specific Registers.
* 🛡️ *eBPF Syscall Monitoring:* High-performance tracepoint attachment (`execve`, `ptrace`, `init_module`, `bpf`) with event polling.
* ⚡ *Lock-Free Ring Buffer:* Inter-process communication via a power-of-two circular buffer residing in shared memory (`/dev/shm`) with zero-overhead synchronization.
* 📌 *Core Isolation & Pinning:* Dedicated CPU affinity management (`sched_setaffinity`) to isolate telemetry execution.
* 🔄 *Deterministic Replay & Verification:* Trace file reconstruction, step-by-step execution, and CRC32 cryptographic hashing for integrity checks.
* 📈 *Multi-Format Reporting:* Automated generation of detailed JSON, stylized HTML (Terminal Dark Theme), and Console reports.

