== 📂 Project Structure

[source,text]
----
.
├── include/
│   └── lz.h                  # Core header definitions and structures
├── src/
│   ├── main.c                # Central orchestrator and CLI argument parser
│   ├── utils/
│   │   ├── logger.c          # High-performance logging subsystem
│   │   └── config.c          # Configuration management
│   ├── core/
│   │   ├── ringbuf.c         # Lock-free shared memory ring buffer
│   │   ├── isolation.c       # Core isolation and CPU pinning
│   │   └── replay.c          # Deterministic replay and CRC32 engine
│   ├── telemetry/
│   │   ├── pmc.c             # Performance monitoring counters
│   │   ├── intel_pt.c        # Intel Processor Trace engine
│   │   └── msr_filter.c      # KVM MSR interception module
│   └── channel/
│       └── ebpf.c            # eBPF tracepoint monitor
│   └── analysis/
│       ├── decode.c          # Intel PT packet stream decoder
│       └── report.c          # JSON, HTML, and Console reporting
├── Makefile                  # Optimized build orchestration
----

---

== ⚙️ Prerequisites

* *OS:* Linux Kernel (x86_64 with Intel PT and KVM support)
* *Compiler:* GCC (with C99/C11 support)
* *Privileges:* Root access or appropriate capabilities (`CAP_SYS_ADMIN`, `CAP_PERFMON`) for hardware telemetry and eBPF tracepoints.

---

== 🛠️ Building & Installation

To build the framework, simply run:

[source,bash]
----
make
----

To install the binary globally on your system:

[source,bash]
----
sudo make install
----

To clean build artifacts:

[source,bash]
----
make clean
----

---

== 💡 Usage

Run `lz --help` to view all available command-line options:

[source,bash]
----
usage: lz [options]
  -h, --help              show this help
  -v, --verbose           verbose logging
  -c, --config FILE       load config file
  -o, --output DIR        output directory (default ./lz_report)
  -l, --log FILE          log file path
  -n, --no-color          disable colored output
  -d, --daemon            run in background
      --iso               enable core isolation
      --ring              enable ring buffer
      --pt                enable Intel PT tracing
      --pmc               enable PMCs
      --msr               enable MSR interception
      --ebpf              enable eBPF syscall monitor
      --replay            enable deterministic replay
      --all               enable all modules
      --shm NAME          shared memory name (default lz_shm)
----

=== 📋 Example Commands

* *Run all security auditing and telemetry modules:*
  [source,bash]
  ----
  sudo ./lz --all --verbose
  ----

* *Run as a background daemon with Intel PT and PMC enabled:*
  [source,bash]
  ----
  sudo ./lz --daemon --pt --pmc -o /var/log/lz_report
  ----

